+/// Offset of the first run of three or more `fence_byte`s at or after `from`.
+///
+/// This is the position [`memmem::Finder::find`] reports for the three-byte
+/// needle: an occurrence of three in a row is exactly the start of a run of at
+/// least three, and the earliest occurrence starts the earliest such run.
+///
+/// The route to it differs. A fenced body is searched from its opening fence
+/// to its closing one, and the byte that delimits the block is by construction
+/// rare inside it, so the first occurrence of a single fence byte is almost
+/// always the closing run itself. That makes a one-byte search the right
+/// shape: it answers in one pass with a plain vector loop, whereas the
+/// three-byte searcher pays to arrange its packed-pair prefilter on entry —
+/// a cost the short hop from an opening fence to its closer cannot amortize,
